From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 23:38:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01184/11171] [conductor] In-process docs for HEURISTIC SEARCH
 OVER THE VERIFIED WORLD MODEL (THE CENTRAL BET of the Deep-Think pivot):
 implement a planning search -- bounded best-first / A* / depth-limited MCTS
 -- over the induced+verifier-certified world model from exp4020, with the
 VERIFIER as the forward simulator (legal next-state expansion + the exp4020
 goal test) and a heuristic value (distance-to-goal proxy: cells-to-goal,
 progress-bar delta, object-alignment, or a learned/coded heuristic) providing
 the directional gradient the verifier cannot. TARGET: break a planning wall
 that single-step re-induce->validate->act STALLED on (r11l L4, or vc33 --
 where a 99%-accurate verified WM still failed to solve). This is the direct
 test of Deep Think Q2 (dynamics != heuristics: does adding a SEPARATE
 navigator over the verified simulator advance past the wall?) AND of the
 modality-mismatch steelman (if search over the code-represented WM SOLVES it,
 the wall was SEARCH not representation -- which our vc33 99%-WM data
 predicts).

Co-Authored-By: Codex CLI <noreply@openai.com>
